  grep -iE 'acpi|lid|battery|ac_adapter|power supply|thermal' | \
  awk '{print substr($0, 1, 16)}' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -20

# Current logind config
grep -vE '^\s*#|^\s*$' /etc/systemd/logind.conf

# What action is set for lid/power button/idle
loginctl show-seat seat0 2>/dev/null
Also look at the pattern across the full 2 weeks — if these bursts always precede IO spikes, case closed:

bash
# How many "Lockdown: systemd-logind" messages per minute, last 2 weeks
journalctl -k --since "2 weeks ago" --no-pager | \
  grep "Lockdown: systemd-logind" | \
  awk '{print $1, $2, $3}' | cut -c1-12 | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -20
Any minute with more than 2 counts is a burst — compare those timestamps to your IO graph.

The fix
Tell logind to stop even trying. Edit /etc/systemd/logind.conf:

bash
nano /etc/systemd/logind.conf
Set (uncomment if needed):

HandleLidSwitch=ignore
HandleLidSwitchExternalPower=ignore
HandleLidSwitchDocked=ignore
HandlePowerKey=ignore
HandleSuspendKey=ignore
HandleHibernateKey=ignore
IdleAction=ignore
Then reload:

bash
systemctl restart systemd-logind
⚠️ Restarting logind will kick any active login sessions (including your SSH session in some configs). Usually fine on Proxmox since shells are under their own scope, but be ready to reconnect.

Also mask the sleep targets outright as a belt-and-braces measure — this is the standard recommendation for servers running on laptop hardware:

bash
systemctl mask sleep.target suspend.target hibernate.target hybrid-sleep.target
Install jq while you're there
For next time:

bash
apt install -y jq
Bottom line: your laptop's ACPI/lid/power subsystem is generating spurious suspend requests. Each one triggers a failed hibernation attempt that cascades into logind activity and correlated IO. Masking the sleep targets and telling logind to ignore all power events will stop it cold. If the bursts continue after that fix, the next layer is identifying which ACPI event is flapping — usually a loose power connector, a dying battery, or a quirky lid sensor.

