promtail DaemonSet (runs on every node) tails those files
     ↓
promtail pushes to loki-0 over HTTP
     ↓
loki-0 writes to storage (your NFS backend, via CSI-NFS)
This is high-volume. Every log line from every container in your cluster flows through this. And with your restart-happy cluster (apiserver 88+ restarts, calico 93 restarts, etc.), there's ton of log spam from container churn.

Path 2: Loki watches Kubernetes events (smaller)
